<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/report.css"><title>Your evidence report</title></head><body><main>
<p class="eyebrow">VisiSocial · evidence report</p><h1>Your data, with its sources.</h1><p><%= identity.name || 'Your account' %> · Posting timezone: <%= report.metadata.timezone %></p>
<% if (demo) { %><p class="notice">Synthetic profile and authored mock providers. These observations are a software demonstration.</p><% } %>
<nav><a href="/consent">Change consent</a> · <a href="/export">Download report JSON</a></nav>
<h2>Module status</h2><ul><% for (const [section, module] of Object.entries(report.modules)) { %><li><strong><%= section %></strong>: <%= module.status %><% if (module.error) { %> (<%= module.error %>)<% } %><% if (Object.keys(module.diagnostics).length) { %><details><summary>Diagnostics</summary><pre><%= JSON.stringify(module.diagnostics, null, 2) %></pre></details><% } %></li><% } %></ul>
<h2>Evidence checklist</h2><% for (const [key, feature] of Object.entries(report.features)) { %><article><h3><%= key %> <span><%= feature.status === 'ok' ? '✓ observed' : 'insufficient evidence' %></span></h3><% if (feature.status === 'ok') { %><pre><%= JSON.stringify(feature.value, null, 2) %></pre><% } %><details><summary>Why am I seeing this?</summary><p>Method: <%= feature.method %> (v<%= feature.methodVersion %>) · n=<%= feature.n %> · confidence: <%= feature.confidence === null ? 'not estimated' : feature.confidence %></p><p>Source IDs: <%= feature.inputs.join(', ') || 'none' %></p><% for (const limit of feature.limitations) { %><p><%= limit %></p><% } %></details></article><% } %>
<% const guesses = report.features['inference.guesses']?.value; if (Array.isArray(guesses)) { %><h2>What could an automated system infer?</h2><% for (const [index, guess] of guesses.entries()) { %><article><p>An AI model guessed <strong><%= guess.attribute %>: <%= guess.guess %></strong>. This is not an established fact.</p><% for (const e of guess.evidence) { %><blockquote><%= e.quote %> (post <%= e.postId %>)</blockquote><% } %><form method="post" action="/feedback"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>"><input type="hidden" name="index" value="<%= index %>"><button class="secondary">This is wrong</button></form></article><% } } %>
<h2>Verified explanations</h2><p>Key and number checks plus a second LLM judge pass. This is not independent human validation.</p><% for (const sentence of report.explanations.sentences) { %><p><%= sentence.text %> <small>Sources: <%= sentence.supportedBy.join(', ') %></small></p><% } %><p>Attempted: <%= report.explanations.attempted %>; dropped: <%= report.explanations.flagged %>; flagged rate: <%= report.explanations.flaggedRate === null ? 'not measured' : report.explanations.flaggedRate %>.</p>
<p>Breach data source, when enabled: <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/">Have I Been Pwned</a>, CC BY 4.0. No breach record does not prove safety or current account existence.</p>
<details><summary>Reproducibility metadata</summary><pre><%= JSON.stringify(report.metadata, null, 2) %></pre></details>
<form method="post" action="/delete"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>"><button class="secondary">Delete my data</button></form><form method="post" action="/logout"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>"><button class="secondary">Log out</button></form>
</main></body></html>
